## Known state of the system (2026-08-10)

Useful as ready-made controls, and as the answer to "has this already been
measured?".

- `+getfwd` in `agentx_owned.list` **actually forwards only for `ifmibdb/` and
  `mxrstpdb/`**. On `mxportdb/` and `stdethdb/` it is a **silent no-op** —
  measured, root cause not found (ADR-0025). Adding it there changes nothing, so
  "no slowdown" there means "nothing happened", not "forwarding is free".
- mxPort `.603.1.1`: mainline **0.768 s** / 154 vb, Plan E **0.681 s** / 193 vb
  (interleaved, 9 reps each). The 0.871 s figure in the 2026-08-09 handoff is an
  outlier. **The whole 2026-08-09 mainline table was not interleaved** — re-measure
  before quoting any row of it.
- mxRstp `.603.3.2`: mainline ~31 s → Plan E 0.63–0.66 s, 25 → 27 MIB objects.
  The 31 s also comes from that un-interleaved batch.
